  "raw_text": "138\n\nBîp tialka laya\n \n(a/t:\n \nBîp tyalka laya\n-\ndict-alt,my\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncow milk\n \n/ leche de vaca\n\nDiwas laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndew\n \n/ rocío\n\nLaya diaia dukiara\n \n(Alt\n(\nbh125\n):\n \nLi di ba\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nwater for drinking, drinking water\n \n/ agua para beber, agua\npotable\n\nLaya tahpla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrum\n \n/ ron\n\n(Lit:\n \nbitter water\n \n/ agua amarga)\n\nNakra laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntears, eye-water, water of the eye\n \n/ lágrimas, agua para los ojos\n\nNasma laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhoney\n \n/ miel\n\nTialka laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmilk\n \n/ leche\n\n(Note/Nota: Is not used to\n \nrefer to coconut milk\n,\n \nbut\n \njust milk from the teat / No se utiliza para referirse a la leche\n\nde coco,\n \npero\n \nsolo la leche de la teta)\n\nTialka laya subaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto milk the teat\n \n/ ordeñar la teta\n\nLî aubaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto flow, to rise (tide), to pull water, to draw water, to absorb water\n \n/ fluir, subir (marea), sacar\nagua, jalar agua, absorber agua\n\nLî aubra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstream of water, flow of water\n \n/ corriente de agua, flujo de agua\n\nLî auhaia\n \n(&\n \nLi auhwaia\n?) (v)\n \n–\n \nto rain\n \n/ llover\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLî auhisa\n \n–\n \nI\nt’s raining\n \n/\n \nEs\ntá lloviendo)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nNahuala, lî ailal auhwi kan\n \n–\n \nYesterday it was raining a lot\n \n/ Ayer estaba lloviendo mucho)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nlî ba takaskras auhwan\n \n–\n \nit rained without stopping\n \n/ llovió sin parar)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nlî auhi ba\n \n–\n \nthe raining, the rainstorm\n \n/ la lluvia, la tormenta)\n\nL\nî\n \nauhka\n \n(\ndb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nrain, rainwater\n \n/ lluvia, agua de lluvia\n\nLî auhras\n \n(\ndb,lfb\n) (v-neg,n/s)\n \n–\n \nnot rain, not raining, drought\n \n/ no llueve, sequía\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLî auhras ba\n \n–\n \nthe drought\n \n/ la sequía)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb48\n):\n \nLî auhras kan piua ra, Jehova Elías ra win: ...\n \n–\n \nAt the time that it was not raining, Jehovah said to\nElijah: ...\n;\n \nAt the time of the drought, Jehovah said to Elijah: ...\n \n/ En el momento en que no estaba lloviendo,\nJehová le dijo a Elías: ...; En el momento de la sequía, Jehová le dijo a Elías: ...)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb46\n):\n \nLî auhras ba yang pâtki apia\n \n–\n \nThe drought is not my fault\n \n/ La sequía no es mi culpa)\n\nL\nî\n \naula\n \n–\n \nrain is (immediately) coming\n \n/ viene la lluvia (inmediatamente)\n\nLî diaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto drink water\n \n/ beber agua\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb47\n):\n \n(Elías) plun pin bara lî din, bara kli yapan.\n \n–\n \n(Elijah) ate food and drank water, and went back to sleep again.\n\n/ (Elías) comió y bebió agua, y se volvió a dormir.)\n\nLî drap aik\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nGive me a little water\n \n/ Dame un poco de agua\n \n(Alt:\n \nLî wira aik\n)\n\nLî iswaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nplace where water comes from, spring, something that leaks water\n \n/ lugar de donde viene el\nagua, manantial, fuente, algo que gotea agua\n\nLî kap kum\n \n–\n \na cup of water\n \n/ un vaso de agua\n\nL\nî\n \nkati\n \n–\n \nJune\n \n/ junio\n\n(Lit:\n \nrain moon\n \n/ luna de lluvia\n)\n\nLî karma\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwater spring, water source, water channel\n \n/ fuente de agua, canal de agua\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb102\n):\n \nJisas, Sîp luhpia ba, sepadka sa bara rayaka laya karma ra tâ brisa.\n \n–\n \nJesus, the Lamb, is (also the) shepherd\nand leads (them) to waters of life.\n \n/\n \nJesús, el Cordero pastorea y los conduce a las aguas de la vida.)\n\nLî kauhla\n \n–\n \ncold water\n \n/ agua fría\n\nLî klaswan\n \n(\ndictu,db\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhail, ice\n \n/ granizo, hielo\n\n(Note/Nota: Sometimes\n \nLî klaswan\n \nis used to translate snow in\n \ndb\n \n/ A veces,\n \nLî klaswan\n \nse usa para traducir\n \nnieve\n \nen\n \ndb\n\nLî plapaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nplace where water flows, something through which water passes, canal, ditch\n \n/ un lugar\ndonde fluye el agua, algo por donde pasa agua, canal, zanha\n\nLî sikwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto drizzle\n \n/ brisar\n\nL\nî\n \ntaim\n \n/\n \nL\nî\n \npiua\n \n–\n \nrainy season\n \n/ temporada de lluvias\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \nMani laptika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndry season\n \n/ estación seca\n)\n\nLiwanhta\n \n(\ndb,dictu,lf\nb\n,\nlmd,\nyc,jl\n;\n \nLiwahnta\n,\nLihunta\n-\ndict\n;\n \na/t:\n \nL\nî\n \nwanhta\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwell (for water\n)\n \n/ pozo (para agua)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb75\n):\n \nJekob\n \nlayawanhta\n \n–\n \nJacob’s well\n \n/ el pozo de Jacob\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb57\n):\n \n(Wihta nani) (Jirimaya) alki liwanhta pakni drapapa ailal bri kan ba ra lulkan\n \n–\n \n(The leaders) capturing\n\n(Jeremiah) threw (him) in a deep well having a lot of mud\n \n/ (Los líderes) capturando a (Jeremías) lo arrojaron a un pozo\n\nprofundo con mucho lodo)\n\nL\nî\n \nwatla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwater container, water jar\n \n/ contenedor de agua, jarra de agua",
